Installation
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Start  this  ARexx door somewhere from "sys.nuser" or "sys.welcome", or any
other  textfile  that  will  be  displayed  to  every caller. Of course you
shouldn't install it before the login sequence, jerk. :)

Use {#0<path>1oo_AutoSig.rexx}, where { is a CTRL-Q and <path> is of course
the path to the door (you did guess that did you).

Thats all!

Actually,  its a door of such high simplicity that writing a .doc for it is
merely  obsolete  :)  -  but  I  don't  like  programs  that  come  with no
documentation at all, so I just once more prove a good example. :)

If  you  don't like the look of the signature, you may hack the tiny little
ARexx  script  and change it to your own liking. If you don't use 16 colors
you  may  change the contained MCI color codes. But please don't remove the
credit  (that  is,  the  name  of  the program and the author), thats all I
request.


Credit
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
All stupid ARexx "programming" by Neurodancer; the BLINK() routine is based
on  PMK's  ingenious  "FPWait.rexx"  animated  wait  prompts.  Note that it
requires "rexxsupport.library" to do the delay() thing.


